  message: "PREREQUISITE MET. INV-larol satisfied at dev d7b069b106: an external-program launch now keeps its opacity through the producer stamp, so a catalogue row that classifies a launch can no longer strip it. That was the blocker on this item — opening the overlay door for uncatalogued languages would otherwise hand the measured false confirm (a six-line curl -> net_send overlay making a script that writes into /etc/cron.d return confirmed rc 0) to any user who wrote the obvious overlay. Both dispositions are now safe to pursue on their own merits. Disposition 2 (warn when an overlay declares a language that resolved to no catalogue) remains the strictly smaller one and is correct even if disposition 1 never happens."  # 458b
